the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base relatesto includes these resources:
    lomo.

the knowledge base relatesto includes:

the text of the source description is at "sources/relatesTo.ttl".

% Who bears a duty: the agent of this role of the action (lomo.le).
the bearer role is addresser.

the texts of "skos:note" have no language.


norm gdpr art 5 principles is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_GDPR_Art5_Principles".

norm gdpr art 5 principles is a constitutive rule.

norm gdpr art 5 principles has the label "GDPR Article 5: Principles relating to processing of personal data".

norm gdpr art 5 principles relates to norm gdpr art 6 lawful basis.

norm gdpr art 5 principles has for "skos:note" the value "Both articles are foundational to the GDPR but neither specifies nor derogates from the other - they establish complementary requirements".

norm gdpr art 5 principles is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_5".


norm gdpr art 6 lawful basis is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_GDPR_Art6_LawfulBasis".

norm gdpr art 6 lawful basis is a constitutive rule.

norm gdpr art 6 lawful basis has the label "GDPR Article 6: Lawfulness of processing".

norm gdpr art 6 lawful basis is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_6".


norm fin rep art 4 data requirements is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_FinRep_Art4_DataRequirements".

norm fin rep art 4 data requirements is a prescriptive rule.

norm fin rep art 4 data requirements has the label "Financial Reporting Regulation Article 4: Data reporting requirements".

norm fin rep art 4 data requirements relates to norm fin rep art 5 data verification.

norm fin rep art 4 data requirements has for "skos:note" the value "Both rules govern financial data quality in the same regulatory framework: Article 4 specifies what to report, Article 5 specifies how to verify; they are complementary but independent requirements".

norm fin rep art 4 data requirements is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/815/art_4".


norm fin rep art 5 data verification is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_FinRep_Art5_DataVerification".

norm fin rep art 5 data verification is a prescriptive rule.

norm fin rep art 5 data verification has the label "Financial Reporting Regulation Article 5: Data verification requirements".

norm fin rep art 5 data verification is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2019/815/art_5".


norm eia art 5 public consultation is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_EIA_Art5_PublicConsultation".

norm eia art 5 public consultation is a prescriptive rule.

norm eia art 5 public consultation has the label "Environmental Impact Assessment Directive Article 5: Public consultation on environmental effects".

norm eia art 5 public consultation relates to norm eia art 6 screening requirements.

norm eia art 5 public consultation has for "skos:note" the value "Both articles are procedural requirements for environmental assessment but neither determines nor overrides the other - they work together in sequence".

norm eia art 5 public consultation is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2014/52/art_5".


norm eia art 6 screening requirements is identified by "http://example.org/Rule_EIA_Art6_ScreeningRequirements".

norm eia art 6 screening requirements is a prescriptive rule.

norm eia art 6 screening requirements has the label "Environmental Impact Assessment Directive Article 6: Screening for environmental effects".

norm eia art 6 screening requirements is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2014/52/art_6".


% The questions of LOMO's requirements document (its competency questions),
% as far as a description can answer them.
query applies is:
    which rule applies to which party.

query rules_without_conditions is:
    which rule has no written conditions.

query places is:
    which rule is laid down in which place.

query kinds is:
    which thing is of the kind which kind.

query rules_of_act is:
    which rule is established by the act which act.

query provisions is:
    which thing is established in which provision.

query joint_rules is:
    which rule is established in more than one provision.

query prescriptive is:
    which thing is a prescriptive rule.

query constitutive is:
    which thing is a constitutive rule.

query related_rules is:
    which rule is related to which second rule.

query parts is:
    which thing is part of the description.

query texts is:
    which thing is described by the text which text.

query other_values is:
    which thing has for which property the value which value.

query addresses is:
    which thing is identified by which address.

query plain_texts is:
    the texts of which property have no language.

query bearer is:
    the bearer role is which role.

